  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="5cdbb604-6720-5ab0-bf3d-1b3bed0abb20" activityNameId="0eb2f259-8d71-5696-aafb-d57a9eaa18b9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Window frame, wood-metal, w/o surface treatment, wall opening, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Window frame, wood-metal, w/o surface treatment, wall opening, at plant
The measures of the window are 1.75m (width) x 1.3m (height). The wall opening is 1.8 m2 (assumption width of frame 0.12m, 2/3 of frame are behind the wall opening). The bill of materials is based on data from 4 window producers.;
UUID: 08214b4f-e1e3-3317-8e1d-d7b2971dc56a
Included are the materials used in a wooden-metal window frame (without surface treatment and metal panelling). Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 window manufacturers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_08214b4f-e1e3-3317-8e1d-d7b2971dc56a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
